Public Works Director
 Description
This is a phased project designed to focus on design for population growth.  Phase I of the project adds a 14,700 square foot pre-engineered metal
building addition on the west side of the existing building to accommodate eight snow plow truck/sander/plows.  Phase I also includes necessary
site work to accommodate the expansion.  A future Phase II project will remodel the existing facility office and common area to include handicap
accessible restrooms, install showers and separate bunk room, and add additional storage.  It will also include relocation and remodel of the
existing tool room.  The existing truck storage area will undergo minimal upgrades in this future phase.
Project #
ST-14-001
 Justification
The Public Works Department is focused on projecting design of a facility capable of supporting the citizens of Cheyenne based on projected 20
