Fire Chief
 Description
Annual replacement of fire hose in smaller quantities, rahter than a lump-sum. This project wourld replace one-tenth (1/10) of the quantity of the
fire hose each year. As fire hose should be replaced every 10 years, this schedule would provide that each fire hose section is retired at the ten year
mark and minimize the need to replace every section at one time.
Project #
FI-16-002
 Justification
Fire hose is an integral part of providing fire protection. Water pressure in the hose may be anywhere from 150 psi to 200 psi, depending on the
amount of water needed to fight the fire conditions. As fire hose ages, the ability to hold higher pressures is reduced and the hose may burst. The
ultimate need for replacing older fire hose is for safety.
